# trefolio Design System

Default trefolio UI uses a restrained glass visual system powered by semantic tokens in `src/app/globals.css`. `canvas`, `terminal`, and `studio` remain supported via token overrides and shared structure parity. Toggle and layout rules come from `useTheme()` in `@/lib/theme-context`.

> Full design system (personas, voice, tokens, components, accessibility): `.cursor/skills/product-manager/design-system.md`

## Core Rules

- Use semantic tokens and shared primitives first: `.card`, `.glass-toolbar`, `.glass-overlay`, `.btn-*`.
- Do not hard-code new `bg-white`, `dark:bg-slate-*`, or one-off gray border stacks when a shared primitive can express the same intent.
- Overlays, drawers, menus, and bottom sheets must be more opaque than decorative cards.
- Charts and dense tables must remain readability-first; decoration belongs around the data, not on top of it.
- Mobile should use calmer layers than desktop hero cards.
- Theme parity still applies: same structure, same features, different token presentation.

## Color Palette (semantic)

- **Page background**: `--page-gradient`, `--page-background`
- **Cards**: `.card`
- **Toolbars / sticky chrome**: `.glass-toolbar`
- **Overlays / sheets / drawers**: `.glass-overlay`
- **Accent (primary)**: `--accent`
- **Positive/Gain**: `text-emerald-600 dark:text-emerald-400`, `bg-emerald-50 dark:bg-emerald-500/10`
- **Negative/Loss**: `text-red-500 dark:text-red-400`, `bg-red-50 dark:bg-red-500/10`
- **Primary text**: `text-[color:var(--foreground)]`
- **Secondary text**: `text-[color:var(--muted)]`
- **Borders**: `border-[color:var(--border)]`

## Components

- **Cards**: Use `.card`
- **Shell chrome**: Use `.glass-toolbar` for nav/header strips
- **Overlays**: Use `.glass-overlay`
- **Buttons**: `.btn-primary`, `.btn-secondary`, `.btn-danger` (auto dark via globals.css)
- **Inputs/selects**: Auto dark via globals.css base styles
- **Pill selectors**: rounded-full, low-opacity glass background, active state tinted by semantic accent
- **Badges**: `rounded` with light bg + matching text — add `dark:bg-{color}-500/10 dark:text-{color}-400 dark:border-{color}-500/20`
- **Modals**: prefer `glass-overlay` and stronger opacity than cards
- **Tables**: keep headers and dense rows more solid than hero surfaces

## Chart Colors

- Axis ticks: use `isDark ? "#94a3b8" : "#9ca3af"` from `useTheme()`
- Axis lines: use `isDark ? "#334155" : "#e5e7eb"`
- Tooltips: readable first; avoid ultra-translucent popovers
- Line colors unchanged (emerald, blue, violet, amber, red work in both themes)

## Dark Mode Rules

- Prefer semantic tokens before adding more `dark:` utilities
- Header no longer needs to stay hard-coded dark navy; it should inherit shell tokens
- Use `useTheme()` hook for dynamic values (charts, inline styles)
- Auth pages (login, signup, etc.) must wrap with `<ThemeProvider>` since they don't go through the main page
- Use `dark:bg-{color}-500/10` for soft colored backgrounds instead of `dark:bg-{color}-900`

## General Rules

- Use `rounded-[20px]` to `rounded-[30px]` for hero/default glass cards, `rounded-full` for pills/badges, and generous button radii
- Prefer soft borders plus depth over heavy separators
- Gain/loss colors: emerald-600 (dark:emerald-400) / red-500 (dark:red-400) for text
